# D-CAW-WAITER-NOTIFIES-A-DRAINING-HOLDER-13-TIMES-A-SECOND: the step the
# record still owes before removal.  Both halves of the change are measured on
# a long drain (tests/queues/caw_poll_resubmit_ab.queue, run cpr: holder rate
# 12.8-13.3/s with both backoffs off, 1.38/s with both on).  What is not yet
# shown is that the backoffs cost nothing on SHORT waits, which the 100 ms
# cadence was tuned for: the waiter's UDP hint re-send keeps 100 ms for the
# first 3 s of a wait (caw_bast_resend_backoff) and the holder's poll keeps
# submitting on every pass for the first 3 s of a conflict
# (caw_poll_resubmit_backoff), so a bench whose waits stay under 3 s should not
# move.  Same build, runtime knobs, 2/disk/caw/direct g2 (test1, test2):
#   X  = caw_bast_resend_backoff=0 caw_poll_resubmit_backoff=0 (the behaviour
#        before the change)
#   P1 = both 1 (the defaults, the change)
# Order X1 P1a P1b X2, each arm on a fresh prep.  Rows: dlm_scaling
# (create+stat+unlink in private dirs), rsync_paired (each node rsyncs its own
# tree), dlm_fairness (every node churns one shared directory: repeated EX
# hand-offs, the waits the cadence serves), dir_reuse_coherency (concurrent
# same-directory creates under reuse churn).
#
# RULES (written before the first lap).  VALID ARM: tests/fleet_set_params.sh
# reads the arm's two values on both nodes before the rows AND (read-only, bare
# names) after them, with one srcversion throughout; every row printed a
# verdict line.  An arm that fails this is VOID and rerun, never graded.
# PREDICTION (P1 unchanged on short waits): every row PASSes in all four arms,
# and for every row each P1 lap's wall is at most 1.15 x the larger of the two
# X walls + 2 s.  REGRESSION: a P1 wall above that line, or a row passing in
# both X arms and failing in a P1 arm: the backoff costs the common case, and a
# new hypothesis comes before removal.  INTEGRITY: a shutdown, BUG, Oops,
# hung-task or Internal error line on either node stops the work and is
# attributed from its own lines first.
#
# Bounds: prep 300 (run.sh prep_cluster, measured 38-99 s on the 2-node
# groups); knobs 60 (fleet_set_params.sh bounds each ssh at 40 s, nodes in
# parallel); rows 1450: manifest budgets dlm_scaling 90 + rsync_paired 60 +
# dlm_fairness 30 + dir_reuse_coherency 120 = 300, plus preflight and the
# marker check, ~10-20 s per run.sh invocation, plus, for each of the two
# throughput rows (dlm_scaling, rsync_paired: run.sh's PERF_ROWS), run.sh's own
# waits before the row starts: the host lock taken exclusive waits for every
# other group's row in flight to end (the longest on this rig while g2e runs
# its path rows is path_fenced_return, 400 s) and host_quiesce then waits up
# to HOST_QUIET_S 45 + HOST_IDLE_MAX_S 120 s, so 2 x 565 = 1130.  The first
# run of this queue (label cawbk, 2026-10-19 08:26Z, ~/src/mxfs-f
# 6C131EEA932C1F7FE3072EC) had a 360 s rows bound: its X1 rows lap was killed
# at 360 s after dlm_fairness 2 s and dlm_scaling 5 s had PASSed, run.sh having
# waited 75 s for the host lock and 39 s quiescing before dlm_scaling, and the
# queue then ended at lap 7; that run is VOID by the rules above (rows without a
# verdict) and is not graded.  Its evidence files keep their cawbk_ names;
# this queue's are cawbk2_.
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 prep_cluster
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff=0 caw_poll_resubmit_backoff=0" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_X1_before.txt
1450 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 dlm_scaling rsync_paired dlm_fairness dir_reuse_coherency
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff caw_poll_resubmit_backoff" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_X1_after.txt
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 prep_cluster
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff=1 caw_poll_resubmit_backoff=1" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_P1a_before.txt
1450 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 dlm_scaling rsync_paired dlm_fairness dir_reuse_coherency
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff caw_poll_resubmit_backoff" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_P1a_after.txt
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 prep_cluster
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff=1 caw_poll_resubmit_backoff=1" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_P1b_before.txt
1450 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 dlm_scaling rsync_paired dlm_fairness dir_reuse_coherency
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff caw_poll_resubmit_backoff" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_P1b_after.txt
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 prep_cluster
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff=0 caw_poll_resubmit_backoff=0" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_X2_before.txt
1450 ./run.sh 2/disk/caw/direct --group g2 dlm_scaling rsync_paired dlm_fairness dir_reuse_coherency
60 tests/fleet_set_params.sh "caw_bast_resend_backoff caw_poll_resubmit_backoff" 2 tests/evidence/cawbk2_X2_after.txt
